---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About — Lead From The Hip"
	description="David Morris on 28 years in HR and leader development, and why this site is where he does the practice himself."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="About"
		standfirst="I'm David Morris. I've spent 28 years in Human Resources, most of it helping leaders build and maintain high performing teams."
	>
		I knew a lot about leadership.<br />
		<span class="accent">It hadn't changed how I showed up.</span>
	</Hero>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<div class="measure flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink">
			<p>
				For the last decade I've designed and run leader development
				programs, from front-line supervisors to senior executives. I've
				administered more assessments and 360s than I can count, and
				coached leaders on what to do with the results.
			</p>
			<p>
				What surprised me: the content was rarely the problem. Most leaders
				have sat through solid programs, read the right books, and gotten
				accurate feedback. What they lack is a simple, repeatable way to
				turn any of it into a daily habit.
			</p>
			<p>
				I was one of them. So this site is where I do the practice myself.
				The three exercises are the ones I run, and most weeks I post on
				Substack how they went: what a colleague said, what showed up in my
				journal, what I changed. Whether it works is there for you to see.
			</p>
			<a
				href="https://substack.com/@leadfromthehip"
				class="self-start bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 my-2 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				Follow on Substack →
			</a>
			<p>
				My background is in measurement: I spent my first seven years
				analyzing jobs and designing tests to predict performance. That
				instinct shapes everything here. Don't assume something worked.
				Ask. Then ask again in ninety days, and let the answer be the answer.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">More about me</h2>
		<ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-1 text-ink">
			<li>
				M.S., Industrial-Organizational Psychology — California State University,
				San Bernardino (2001)
			</li>
			<li>Hogan Assessment Systems — certified in the HPI, HDS, and MVPI (2020)</li>
			<li>
				<a
					href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/david-c-morris-6b21a01"
					class="text-petrol underline hover:opacity-80 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
				>
					LinkedIn
				</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">Get in touch</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure mb-6">
			Start with a twenty-minute call to see whether there's anything here for
			you.
		</p>
		<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center">
			<a
				href="https://calendar.app.google/VMSWBtEeNv131AxA6"
				class="bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				Book a call →
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
